# Values on a deep mixed path (the author, CODEX-AUTHOR-PATH-VALUES-20261018T222137Z): a nested Structure, a reference field
# crossed, an indexed element; a read; a write, then a read of the changed place AND of its untouched neighbours; an address
# taken, written through, the field read back by its path.  The neighbours carry distinct values (p 11, q 22, r 33; arr
# 100..103; vals 200..202) so a wrong slot, index or map shows as a wrong number, never as a coincidence.  One COMBINED
# route as well (Codex CODEX-U7D2-READONLY-20261019T024937Z): names, the reference crossed, then an index on the
# referenced Structure's Array field -- `A\mid\ref\vals[i]` -- read, written with its neighbours read back, its element's
# address taken and written through.  Natively and with the methods walked.  Success 7; 81 first read, 82 reference
# write/neighbours, 83 element write/neighbours, 84 address, 86 combined read, 87 combined write/neighbours, 89 combined
# element address.
C:
    int: p 11
    int: q 22
    int: r 33
    []: int vals 3
end: C
A:
    mid:
        @: ref C
        []: int arr 4
        int: tag 3
    end: mid
end: A
fn: fill () int
    A\mid\arr[0]: 100
    A\mid\arr[1]: 101
    A\mid\arr[2]: 102
    A\mid\arr[3]: 103
    A\mid\ref\vals[0]: 200
    A\mid\ref\vals[1]: 201
    A\mid\ref\vals[2]: 202
    return: 0
end: fill
fn: probe () int
    @: pq int
    @: pv int
    fill()
    if: A\mid\ref\q != 22 || A\mid\arr[2] != 102 || A\mid\ref\r + A\mid\tag != 36
        return: 81
    A\mid\ref\q: 44
    A\mid\arr[2]: 55
    if: A\mid\ref\q != 44 || A\mid\ref\p != 11 || A\mid\ref\r != 33
        return: 82
    if: A\mid\arr[1] != 101 || A\mid\arr[2] != 55 || A\mid\arr[3] != 103
        return: 83
    pq: @ A\mid\ref\q
    \pq: 66
    if: A\mid\ref\q != 66 || A\mid\ref\p != 11
        return: 84
    if: A\mid\ref\vals[1] != 201 || A\mid\ref\vals[0] + A\mid\ref\vals[2] != 402
        return: 86
    A\mid\ref\vals[1]: 77
    if: A\mid\ref\vals[0] != 200 || A\mid\ref\vals[1] != 77 || A\mid\ref\vals[2] != 202 || A\mid\ref\q != 66
        return: 87
    pv: @ A\mid\ref\vals[2]
    \pv: 88
    if: A\mid\ref\vals[2] != 88 || A\mid\ref\vals[1] != 77 || \pv != 88
        return: 89
    return: 7
end: probe
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: probe(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
